      "id": "white",
      "name": "Panda",
      "description": "The coat is confined to the eyes, muzzle, ears, forequarters and hindquarters and everything else goes white, mane and tail included. The eye patches are a little stylised; muzzle and ear markings are optional. Freckles of coat run along the topline - small, or larger and fawn-like. The edges of the coloured regions are smooth: nothing about Panda is jagged or roaned. It never reaches the cheek, the neck or the barrel, and no other marking shows on the white - whatever else the horse carries, it can only be seen where the coat survives.",
